      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "A strong realist argument would definitely frame the immediate removal of Gaddafi as a strategic success, as ending his regime addressed a clear, immediate power projection threat in the Mediterranean. Proponents of this view would argue that the primary objective of regime change, in this case, was achieved, fulfilling a short-term national interest. However, realists must also contend with the \"blowback\" of state failure, which effectively undermined the long-term stability benefits of the intervention.",
      "source": "target",
